<article class="env-lemma" id="0688">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0688">Lemma <span data-tag="0688">37.61.3</span>.</a> A flat base change of a perfect morphism is perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This translates into the following algebra result: Let $A \to B$ be a perfect ring map. Let $A \to A'$ be flat. Then $A' \to B \otimes _ A A'$ is perfect. This result for pseudo-coherent ring maps we have seen in Lemma <a href="/tag/0680" data-tag="0680">37.60.3</a>. The corresponding fact for finite tor dimension follows from More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/066M" data-tag="066M">15.68.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>